    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44461.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "Hi, everyone, and welcome to Washington Post Live. I'm Mariana Sotomayor, congressional reporter at the Washington Post, where we continue to mark Hispanic Heritage Month as part of our Race in America series. There's no one better to talk about her Latinidad and how she brings it to politics and the hallways of Congress than Congresswoman Veronica Escobar of Texas. Congresswoman, thank you so much for joining us today.",
