    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 44461,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44461.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "I wish we had seen that memo sooner. And I so wish that Senator Manchin and Senator Cinema would have begun these conversations with all of us sooner. We're one family. We've got to work together in a transparent way to advance this important agenda to really meet the moment of all the needs that we see across the country and the needs that our communities are carrying. You know, from my perspective, the number is not necessarily what's so important, you know, however many trillions of dollars. I've never really focused on the number, not in the transportation infrastructure bill, not on reconciliation. I really focus far more on what's in the package. And so there's a lot of different ways to slice this. You know, it depends on the length of programs who's included in the programs. But we have to make sure we don't leave immigrants behind. We have to make sure that we adequately and urgently address the climate crisis. We want women to have a shot at prosperity in our economy. And that means childcare. That means funding the care economy. That means uplifting those wages. So, you know, for me, it's more about what we put in it than the final price tag. And I know we can pay for it. And we will pay for it, so we'll do this responsibly.",
