    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "is a Plan C that obviously is not as robust or as it's not what we want. And so we actually had a meeting, Congressman Adriana Espaillat and I are the two co-chairs of the Congressional Hispanic Caucus Task Force that is focused on getting immigration through reconciliation and getting it across the goal line. Here's my view, Mariana, on the parliamentarians' perspective. Her ruling is really just a recommendation. We in the House went through a markup of the legislation that will be included in reconciliation. We have done all of our homework. There is historic precedence for getting immigration in on the Senate side through reconciliation that meets the bird rule. At the end of the day, it is my hope that the Senate will pass a reconciliation package with our full immigration package and that they acknowledge both the recommendation by the parliamentarian, which is non-binding, and they recognize and acknowledge all of the precedent that has been set before in passing immigration changes through reconciliation in the past. And so TBD, let's see what happens, but I am definitely in favor of making sure that we don't leave immigrants behind. You know, we are still in the midst of a global pandemic, but in the darkest of days, who was with us? Who was it that was making sure that we had food on our table? Despite the terrible personal risk to their health and their safety, it was mostly immigrants. And so we've got to stand with them. They've been waiting for decades for this moment. We cannot let this moment pass them or our country by. So I",
