  {
    "episode_id": 44461,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44461.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "You know, you mentioned a little bit about your own upbringing. I know that you grew up on a dairy farm, and you've also made your way to be a county judge throughout your career. And I'm just curious, because growing up, you don't see many women, many people of color necessarily in government, what aspired or made you want to serve in public office? And what is your advice to young Latinas who one day want to run for office?",
