  {
    "episode_id": 44461,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44461.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 29,
    "turn_text": "You mentioned that support that you have, whether it's from friends or even your own community. We all, of course, remember just a couple of years ago, El Paso faced just harrowing and traumatizing face and experience just like that after a gunman went in with racial intent to try and target the Hispanic community. How is your community dealing with this? It obviously takes some time. How are you all leaning on each other? And I think what is the message to the rest of the country that this is something that you all continue to face?",
